<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Fourteenth Dynasty of Egypt</h1><p class="st-meta">1725 BCE – 1650 BCE (approx.) · capital Avaris</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A line of Delta kings of largely Canaanite descent who ruled the eastern Nile Delta as the Middle Kingdom weakened.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>As the Thirteenth Dynasty lost its grip, around 1725 BCE a separate line of kings established itself in the eastern Delta, probably at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avaris">Avaris</a> (Tell el-Dab'a), where a large population of Levantine origin had settled. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manetho">Manetho</a> placed the dynasty at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xois">Xois</a> in the western Delta, but most scholars now locate it at Avaris.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Very little is known. The best-attested king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nehesy">Nehesy</a>, whose name means 'the Nubian', left monuments at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avaris">Avaris</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tell-el-muqdam">Tell el-Muqdam</a> and honoured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seth">Seth</a> as lord of Avaris. Scarabs with royal names suggest a series of short reigns. The dynasty controlled the Delta's trade with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a>, and its population buried their dead in Canaanite fashion, with donkeys and bronze weapons.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The kingdom seems to have been weakened by famine and plague, and around 1650 BCE it was replaced by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/fifteenth-dynasty-of-egypt">Hyksos</a> rulers of the Fifteenth Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, who also made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avaris">Avaris</a> their capital.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/fourteenth-dynasty-of-egypt.jpg" alt="Fourteenth Dynasty of Egypt" width="320" height="370"><figcaption>Image: Iry-Hor · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:14th_dynasty_territory.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1725 BCE – 1650 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century-bce">18th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century-bce">17th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Avaris</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Nehesy</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Egyptian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Egyptian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Fourteenth Dynasty, Xoite Dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1688&amp;focus=fourteenth-dynasty-of-egypt" aria-label="Fourteenth Dynasty of Egypt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5504 1055 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Fourteenth Dynasty of Egypt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5824 1311L5813 1353M5824 1311L5824 1311"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5813 1353h0M5824 1311h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5824 1311h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5824 1311h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Avaris. <a href="/atlas?year=-1688&amp;focus=fourteenth-dynasty-of-egypt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
